{"records":[{"id":"ts44bfg45k","title":"IWS1 phosphorylation promotes cell proliferation and predicts poor prognosis in EGFR mutant lung adenocarcinoma patients, through the cell cycle-regulated U2AF2 RNA splicing_images_depository","description":"Our previous studies have shown that IWS1 (Interacts with Spt6) is a phosphorylation target of Akt and regulates the alternative RNA splicing of FGFR-2, linking IWS1 with lung cancer tumorigenesis. To further address the role of IWS1 in alternative RNA splicing and lung cancer, we performed an RNA-seq study using lung adenocarcinoma cells in which IWS1 was knocked down or replaced by its phosphorylation site mutant. This identified the splicing factor U2 Associated-Factor 2 (U2AF2) as a target of IWS1 phosphorylation, by showing that the loss of phosphorylated IWS1 results in U2AF2 transcripts lacking exon 2. Exon 2 encodes part of the U2AF65 Serine-Rich (SR) Domain, which is required for its binding with pre-mRNA Processing factor 19 (Prp19). Here, we show that the loss of phosphorylated IWS1 interferes with histone H3K36 trimethylation and the assembly of LEDGF/SRSF1 splicing complexes on the U2AF2 gene in a cell-cycle specific manner. The latter results in the downregulation of cell cycle division associated 5  (CDCA5), a phosphorylation target of ERK, leading to impaired cell proliferation, G2/M phase arrest and impaired tumor growth in mouse xenografts models, an effect more pronounced in cells harboring EGFR mutations. Analysis of human lung adenocarcinoma samples reveals robust correlations between IWS1 phosphorylation, U2AF2 splicing pattern, and CDCA5/p-ERK levels, especially in EGFR mutated patients. More importantly, IWS1 phosphorylation is positively correlated with tumor stage and grade and defines poor prognosis in lung adenocarcinoma patients, harboring EGFR, and not KRAS, mutations. This work highlights the instrumental role of the AKT/p-IWS1 axis to alternative RNA splicing in governing cell cycle progression and tumorigenesis, and proposes this axis as a novel drug target and prognosis factor in lung adenocarcinoma, by concomitantly affecting the epigenetic regulation of RNA processing and oncogenic signals.\nThese data accompany the main dataset of our paper  : doi: 10.17632/y82yx8gfkj.3\nIn this dataset, we will upload all the images from cell transformation assays and IHC from mouse xenografts and human samples.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-12-14T10:19:12.319Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ts44bfg45k","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ts44bfg45k"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Georgios","last_name":"Laliotis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Evangelia","last_name":"Chavdoula","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Philip N.","last_name":"Tsichlis","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Applied Sciences"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"mtrfthzdd3","title":"FOSL1 IP western blot","description":"We used A549, a KRAS mutant human lung adenocarcinoma cell line, cells in which FOSL1 was FLAG tagged. We extracted nuclear protein from these cells and immunoprecipitated (IP) the FLAG-tagged protein while using the extract from WT A549 cells as a control. Western Blot images showing the detection of Flag tag and FOSL1 protein.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-12-22T08:58:43.117Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/mtrfthzdd3","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/mtrfthzdd3"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Preetish","last_name":"Kadur Lakshminarasimha Murthy","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"wkxtjpf5dz","title":"siKRAS in H441","description":"This dataset contains fq data of  RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) results from an experiment investigating the effects of KRAS knockdown in H441 lung adenocarcinoma cells. This dataset contains RNA-seq results of KRAS knockdown using siKRAS.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-03-16T11:46:54.013Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/wkxtjpf5dz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/wkxtjpf5dz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mengdi","last_name":"Li","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["RNA Sequencing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4mb5kjywkj","title":"Western Blot raw data of the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\"","description":"The raw images of WB is for the reviewers' request when reviewing the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-12-04T00:26:32.621Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4mb5kjywkj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4mb5kjywkj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mingang","last_name":"Hao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"y82yx8gfkj","title":"IWS1 phosphorylation promotes cell proliferation and predicts poor prognosis in EGFR mutant lung adenocarcinoma patients, through the cell cycle-regulated U2AF2 RNA splicing.","description":"Our previous studies have shown that IWS1 (Interacts with Spt6) is a phosphorylation target of Akt and regulates the alternative RNA splicing of FGFR2, linking IWS1 with lung cancer tumorigenesis. To further address the role of IWS1 in alternative RNA splicing and lung cancer, we performed an RNA-seq study using lung adenocarcinoma cells in which IWS1 was knocked down or replaced by its phosphorylation site mutant. This identified the splicing factor U2 Associated-Factor 2 (U2AF2) as a target of IWS1 phosphorylation, by showing that the loss of phosphorylated IWS1 results in U2AF2 transcripts lacking exon 2. Exon 2 encodes part of the U2AF65 Serine-Rich (SR) Domain, which is required for its binding with pre-mRNA Processing factor 19 (Prp19). Here, we show that the loss of phosphorylated IWS1 interferes with histone H3K36 trimethylation and the assembly of LEDGF/SRSF1 splicing complexes on the U2AF2 gene in a cell-cycle specific manner. The latter results in the downregulation of cell cycle division associated 5  (CDCA5), a phosphorylation target of ERK, leading to impaired cell proliferation, G2/M phase arrest and impaired tumor growth in mouse xenografts models, an effect more pronounced in cells harboring EGFR mutations. Analysis of human lung adenocarcinoma samples reveals robust correlations between IWS1 phosphorylation, U2AF2 splicing pattern, and CDCA5/p-ERK levels, especially in EGFR mutated patients. More importantly, IWS1 phosphorylation is positively correlated with tumor stage and grade and defines poor prognosis in lung adenocarcinoma patients, harboring EGFR, and not KRAS, mutations. This work highlights the instrumental role of the AKT/p-IWS1 axis to alternative RNA splicing in governing cell cycle progression and tumorigenesis, and proposes this axis as a novel drug target and prognosis factor in lung adenocarcinoma, by concomitantly affecting the epigenetic regulation of RNA processing and oncogenic signals.\nThe purpose of this database is to provide all the raw data materials that have led to the conclusions shown in this report. These materials include Western blotting images, PCR images, qPCR raw data and any other raw data material from resources such as plate readers.\nThe cell imaging from IHC and cell cultures will be included in a separate dataset due to size.\nAlong with that, the complete lab book from the whole process will be provided, showing all the procedures followed during the analysis.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-12-22T07:12:10.747Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y82yx8gfkj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y82yx8gfkj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Georgios I.","last_name":"Laliotis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Evangelia","last_name":"Chavdoula","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Maria D.","last_name":"Paraskevopoulou","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Abdul K.","last_name":"Kaba","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Alessandro","last_name":"La Ferlita","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Satish","last_name":"Singh","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Vollter","last_name":"Anastas","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Keith A.","last_name":"Nair II","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Arturo","last_name":"Orlacchio","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Vasiliki","last_name":"Taraslia","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ioannis","last_name":"Vlachos","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Marina","last_name":"Capece","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Artemis","last_name":"Hatzigeorgiou","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Dario","last_name":"Palmieri","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christos","last_name":"Tsatsanis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Salvatore","last_name":"Alaimo","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Lalit","last_name":"Sehgal","orcid":null},{"first_name":"David P.","last_name":"Carbone","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Vincenzo","last_name":"Coppola","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Philip N.","last_name":"Tsichlis","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Biology","Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"6rdzdjp624","title":"KrasG12D/+ co-mutation alters the landscape of lung adenocarcinoma","description":"Tumor pieces from Kras-mutant genetically engineered lung adenocarcinoma mouse models with loss Lkb1 and/or Keap1 were assessed. \nSteady-state LC-MS analysis (M03818) was performed on tumor pieces; or normal lung pieces. Location is annotated.\n13C,15N-Glutamine 15 minute pulse-labeling (M04050) of mice was performed at defined timepoints when tumor burden is known to be significantly progressed. Tumor pieces and plasma were isolated from n=5 mice/genotype.\nRelated to manuscript: \nBest et al., Glutaminase inhibition impairs CD8 T cell activation in STK11/Lkb1 deficient lung cancer. Cell Metabolism, 2022","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-04-21T17:35:47.282Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/6rdzdjp624","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/6rdzdjp624"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Sarah","last_name":"Best","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kate","last_name":"Sutherland","orcid":null},{"first_name":"David ","last_name":"Pirman","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Joshua","last_name":"Goldford","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gillian","last_name":"Kingsbury","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Katie","last_name":"Sellers","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yashira","last_name":"Negrón Abril","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Metabolomics","15Nitrogen Labeling"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3cy28w7v9k","title":"RNA-seq profiling of 634T murine KP NSCLC cells deleted for AMPK subjected to no glucose conditions","description":"This dataset was generated for the paper, \"Genetic analysis reveals AMPK is required to support tumor growth in murine Kras-dependent lung cancer models.\"  Murine Kras mutant, p53 null (KP) 634T NSCLC cells were subjected to the CRISPR/Cas9 system including either a control gRNA (“WT”), or a gRNA targeting both AMPKalpha1 and AMPKalpha2 resulting in AMPK knockout in a polyclonal pooled cell population (“KO”). \"R1\" indicates Replicate 1, \"R2\" indicates Replicate 2. These cells were subjected to no glucose (0mM, \"NG\") conditions for 16 hours, and profiled by RNA-sequencing. \n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-01-10T16:47:21.29Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3cy28w7v9k","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3cy28w7v9k"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lillian","last_name":"Eichner","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Reuben","last_name":"Shaw","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Lung Cancer","RNA Sequencing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"gj763hyrny","title":"RNA-seq profiling of 368T1 murine KP NSCLC cells deleted for AMPK with AMPKa1 add-back subjected to high glucose conditions, Replicate 1","description":"This dataset was generated for the paper, \"Genetic analysis reveals AMPK is required to support tumor growth in murine Kras-dependent lung cancer models.\"  Murine Kras mutant, p53 null (KP) 368T1 NSCLC cells were deleted for AMPK using the CRISPR/Cas9 system and subsequently stably infected with control vector (\"KO\") or AMPKalpha1 cDNA (\"A1\") add-back. These cells were subjected to high glucose (25mM, \"HG\") conditions for 12 or 18 hours, and profiled by RNA-sequencing. Replicate 1 High Glucose (HG) and No Glucose (NG) conditions were generated simultaneously and analyzed together. Analysis of a single dataset was performed using Replicate 1 (\"R1\"), and both replicates (\"R1\" and \"R2\") were analyzed together as indicated.   ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-01-10T16:46:02.47Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/gj763hyrny","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/gj763hyrny"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lillian","last_name":"Eichner","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Reuben","last_name":"Shaw","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Lung Cancer","RNA Sequencing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"fvy29f2ptz","title":"RNA-seq profiling of 368T1 murine KP NSCLC cells deleted for AMPK with AMPKa1 add-back subjected to high glucose conditions, Replicate 2","description":"This dataset was generated for the paper, \"Genetic analysis reveals AMPK is required to support tumor growth in murine Kras-dependent lung cancer models.\"  Murine Kras mutant, p53 null (KP) 368T1 NSCLC cells were deleted for AMPK using the CRISPR/Cas9 system and subsequently stably infected with control vector (\"KO\") or AMPKalpha1 cDNA (\"A1\") add-back. These cells were subjected to high glucose (25mM, \"HG\") conditions for 12 or 18 hours, and profiled by RNA-sequencing. Replicate 2 High Glucose (HG) and No Glucose (NG) conditions were generated simultaneously and analyzed together. Analysis of a single dataset was performed using Replicate 1 (\"R1\"), and both replicates (\"R1\" and \"R2\") were analyzed together as indicated.   ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-11-02T22:56:14.317Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/fvy29f2ptz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/fvy29f2ptz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lillian","last_name":"Eichner","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Reuben","last_name":"Shaw","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Lung Cancer","RNA Sequencing"],"journal_issn":["15504131"]},{"id":"3tygtgw7mz","title":"RNA-seq profiling of 368T1 murine KP NSCLC cells deleted for AMPK with AMPKa1 add-back subjected to no glucose conditions, Replicate 2","description":"This dataset was generated for the paper, \"Genetic analysis reveals AMPK is required to support tumor growth in murine Kras-dependent lung cancer models.\"  Murine Kras mutant, p53 null (KP) 368T1 NSCLC cells were deleted for AMPK using the CRISPR/Cas9 system and subsequently stably infected with control vector (\"KO\") or AMPKalpha1 cDNA (\"A1\") add-back. These cells were subjected to no glucose (0mM, \"NG\") conditions for 12 or 18 hours, and profiled by RNA-sequencing. Replicate 2 High Glucose (HG) and No Glucose (NG) conditions were generated simultaneously and analyzed together. Analysis of a single dataset was performed using Replicate 1 (\"R1\"), and both replicates (\"R1\" and \"R2\") were analyzed together as indicated.   ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-11-02T22:56:00.303Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3tygtgw7mz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3tygtgw7mz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lillian","last_name":"Eichner","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Reuben","last_name":"Shaw","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Lung Cancer","RNA Sequencing"],"journal_issn":["15504131"]}],"total_records":111451,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":131,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":111451,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":110981,"restricted":57,"embargoed":413},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":1949},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":568},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":436},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":380},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":376},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":365},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":343},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":295},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":237},{"id":"https://ror.org/00k4n6c32","name":"European Commission","count":202}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":108914},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1888},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Resea